<title>GERMANY: LUGE-RESULTS FROM ALTENBERG WORLD CUP EVENT.</title>
<headline>LUGE-RESULTS FROM ALTENBERG WORLD CUP EVENT.</headline>
<dateline>ALTENBERG, Germany 1996-12-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results of women's</p>
<p>competition at World Cup event in Altenberg on Saturday:</p>
<p> 1. Jana Bode (Germany)		    One minute 27.224 seconds</p>
<p>(43.559/43.665).</p>
<p> 2. Silke Kraushaar (Germany)	    1:27.281 (43.569/43.712).</p>
<p> 3. Andrea Tagwerker (Austria)	   1:27.403 (43.610/43.793).</p>
<p> 4. Angelika Neuner (Austria)	    1:27.494 (43.699/43.795).</p>
<p> 5. Susi Erdmann (Germany)		 1:27.529 (43.730/43.799).</p>
<p> 6. Gerda Weissensteiner (Italy)	 1:27.565 (43.725/43.840).</p>
<p> 7. Camy Myler (U.S.)			1:27.665 (43.842/43.823).</p>
<p> 8. Natalja Obkircher (Italy)	    1:28.346 (44.275/44.071).</p>
<p>9. Maria Jasencakova (Czech Republic) 1:28.372 (44.252/44.220).</p>
<p> 10. Julia Ludan (Ukraine)		 1:28.597 (44.277/44.320)</p>
<p>World Cup standings after three events:</p>
<p>1. Kraushaar 102 points</p>
<p>2. Tagwerker 90</p>
<p> 3. Neuner    88</p>
<p> 4. Bode	87</p>
<p> 5. Myler     80</p>
